ZGeo change log
===============

Version 1.24.0 — 2026-11-12
Previous GitHub release: v1.22.0 (2026-11-11)

Overview
--------
ZGeo 1.24.0 adds optional checks for geometry validity and coordinate
sanity, restores format-specific size refinement for SHP and MIF/MID, and
brings the checks window to 15 checks. All new checks are optional and
disabled by default, so the existing default workflow is unchanged.

Changes since v1.22.0
---------------------

1.23.0
- Restored the separate "Refine SHP size" and "Refine MIF/MID size"
  checks, placed directly after "Refine size".
- Both format-specific size checks are optional and disabled by default.
- "Refine size" remains first and is enabled by default. It covers all
  formats and takes precedence, so selected formats are not processed
  twice.
- The checks window grew from 11 to 13 checks.

1.24.0
- Added the "Geometry validity check":
  - self-intersections;
  - unclosed rings;
  - empty geometries;
  - null geometries.
- Added the "Coordinate check":
  - NaN and infinite coordinates;
  - excessively large coordinates;
  - swapped latitude and longitude;
  - coordinates outside the valid CRS range.
- For projected CRSs, coordinates are transformed to EPSG:4326 and also
  checked against the CRS area of use.
- Both new checks are optional and disabled by default.
- The checks window now shows 15 checks.
- Updated Russian and English labels, descriptions, tests and
  documentation.

What changed in 1.24.0 compared with 1.22.0
-------------------------------------------
- Added "Refine SHP size" and "Refine MIF/MID size" as optional checks.
- Added "Geometry validity check" and "Coordinate check".
- The checks dialog was enlarged to fit 15 checks.
- The checks tooltip now mentions format-specific size refinement,
  geometry and coordinate checks.
- All problem-check findings continue to be collected in the "Issues"
  column with details in the cell tooltip, the "Problem files: N" counter
  and the "Only problem files" filter.
- Updated unit tests and QGIS smoke tests.

Available checks in 1.24.0
--------------------------
Refinement:
- Refine size (first, default; all formats)
- Refine SHP size (optional)
- Refine MIF/MID size (optional)
- Refine CRS
- Refine feature count

Validation and problem checks:
- Check JSON for GeoJSON format
- Attribute field name check (non-Latin characters)
- Shapefile field name check
- Truncated field name duplicates check
- DBF encoding and .cpg check
- Dataset completeness check
- CRS check
- Geometry validity check
- Coordinate check
- Empty layers check

Compatibility
-------------
- QGIS 3.16 and newer, including QGIS 4 / Qt 6.
- Python 3.9+.
- Windows is the primary target; the plugin uses QGIS and PyQt APIs.

Installation
------------
1. Download `zgeo-1.24.0.zip`.
2. In QGIS open Plugins → Manage and Install Plugins → Install from ZIP.
3. Select the downloaded archive and restart QGIS if it was running.

